---

11. VERIFICATION STANDARD

Before declaring a task complete, run the actual verification sequence.

Minimum applicable checks:

pnpm format:check
pnpm lint
pnpm typecheck
pnpm test
pnpm build

For projects using different tooling, use the equivalent commands.

The verification must occur AFTER the latest code change.

A test run from an older commit is not evidence for the new change.


---

12. EXACT COMPLETION RULE

Use these status terms precisely.

Proposed

Designed but not implemented.

Changed

Source files were edited.

No claim that the change works.

Integrated

All related files and systems have been updated consistently.

Verified Locally

Required local verification passed after the latest change.

CI Green

Complete CI pipeline passed against the exact latest commit.

Complete

Only when:

Requirements are satisfied.

Acceptance criteria pass.

Relevant tests pass.

Build succeeds.

Security checks pass where applicable.

Performance checks pass where applicable.

Documentation is updated.

No known unresolved release blocker remains.



---

13. NO FALSE COMPLETION CLAIMS

Never say:

"This should work."

"Looks correct."

"Implementation complete."


unless the required evidence exists.

If something is unverified, say:

Status: Changed but not verified.

If something is blocked:

Status: Blocked.
Reason:
Required information/access/tool is unavailable.

Never hide unresolved problems.


