One important correction to your original idea

[Certain] "Every project should start without proper full planning and documentation first" should be changed to:

> Every project must begin with sufficient planning and documentation before implementation.



Not necessarily "full documentation."

There is a difference.

A two-week planning process for a simple landing page is wasteful.

A two-hour implementation of an enterprise healthcare system without architecture documentation is reckless.

The correct rule is proportional planning, mandatory documentation, and no blind coding.

That aligns with NEWAX's existing execution philosophy: structured, reliable, transparent, efficient, and adaptable. 

